{"case_id":"C048","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","input semantics","state initialization"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["fuzz/c/std/gif_fuzzer.c:fuzz","fuzz/c/std/zlib_fuzzer.c:fuzz","wuffs_gif__decoder__check_wuffs_version","wuffs_zlib__decoder__check_wuffs_version"],"reason":"S1 reverses the semantic order of the initializer arguments to sizeof_star_self followed by wuffs_version, but both H0 harnesses still pass WUFFS_VERSION followed by sizeof dec. Those values are implicitly convertible, so the calls can compile while initializing the decoders with incorrect arguments. The new first check compares sizeof(*self) with the value supplied as WUFFS_VERSION, causing initialization to fail before normal GIF or zlib decoding is exercised. S0 expected exactly the order used by H0, so the commit introduced this material harness gap.","evidence":["gif_fuzzer.c calls wuffs_gif__decoder__check_wuffs_version(&dec, WUFFS_VERSION, sizeof dec), while S1 declares it as (self, size_t sizeof_star_self, uint32_t wuffs_version).","zlib_fuzzer.c calls wuffs_zlib__decoder__check_wuffs_version(&dec, WUFFS_VERSION, sizeof dec), while S1 declares it as (self, size_t sizeof_star_self, uint32_t wuffs_version).","In S1, both initializer implementations first test sizeof(*self) != sizeof_star_self and set ERROR_BAD_SIZEOF_RECEIVER, so H0's WUFFS_VERSION argument is interpreted as the receiver size.","In S0, the declarations accepted wuffs_version before sizeof_star_self, matching both H0 call sites."],"recommended_action":"Update both H0 initializer calls to pass sizeof dec before WUFFS_VERSION so fuzzing reaches wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_config/decode_frame and wuffs_zlib__decoder__decode under valid initialized state."}
